664: +#### The DOM API counts too
665: +
666: +The rule above is about the *value*, not about the syntax that carried it. Setting
667: +the same literal through the DOM API is equally prohibited: `el.style.cssText`,
668: +`el.style.color`, `el.style.background` and every sibling. This is not a
669: +hypothetical. #854 normalised the attribute form and left the DOM-API form
