295-// ── gdx-2: type-scale floor audit (AC1, AC2, AC3, AC5) ─────────────────────────
296-//
297:// These tests deliberately do NOT use setupSuite(). That helper waits on #app
298-// becoming visible and is the root cause of this file's 12 documented
299-// pre-existing failures. Stylesheets are <link>ed in <head>, so
300-// document.styleSheets is fully populated on a bare page.goto('/') with no app
301-// boot required.
302-
303-const GDX2_SHEETS = ['/css/suite.css', '/css/components.css'];
304-
305-// Selectors deliberately left below the floor by gdx-2 Task 3: the
306-// components.css EDITOR section (its lines 143 to 511) renders admin.html's
307-// character editor, a denser surface outside Epic GDX's player-facing remit.
308-// They were converted px -> rem but keep their authored values.
309-//
310-// This list is a RATCHET, not a wishlist. It was generated from the selectors
311-// actually skipped at the time of the conversion. Any NEW sub-floor selector,
312-// anywhere in either stylesheet, fails the test. A selector-prefix heuristic
313-// cannot replace it: 'sh-' prefixed rules exist on both sides of the carve-out
314-// boundary.
315-//
316-// gdx-2 review patch: the list is now every editor-section declaration below the
317-// 0.75rem BODY floor, not just those below the 0.6875rem micro floor, because the
318-// floor check became role-aware (see gdx2FloorViolation). It went from 68 entries
319-// to 110. Every one of the 110 was confirmed to live inside components.css lines
320-// 143 to 511; suite.css contributes zero, which is the whole point of the
321-// player-scoped override block at the end of that file.
322-//
323-// It is also href-aware now (see gdx2Allowed). An allowlisted selector is a
324-// legitimate carve-out ONLY when it comes from components.css. The same selector
325-// text appearing sub-floor in suite.css means the player-scoped override block
326-// has been deleted or broken, which must fail loudly rather than pass silently.
327-//
328-// Note: the subset of these rules that DOES reach the player sheet (via the
329-// shRender* helpers public/js/suite/sheet.js imports from editor/sheet.js, and
330-// via public/js/tabs/archive-tab.js calling the editor's whole renderSheet) is
331-// raised to the floor by that override block, so index.html never renders them
332-// below the floor. GDX2_PLAYER_OVERRIDES below asserts that positively.
--
